From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:09:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Put the menus on the top screen

The menus and their questions are drawn on their own, between
VID_BeginMenu and VID_EndMenu, on a transparent background (255), which
the video driver shows on the top screen over the view, which the
renderer dims, instead of fading the screen behind them, so the screen
isn't drawn again under them every frame. A page is only drawn again
when it changes: M_PageChanged first runs M_Draw with the draw functions
hashing what they would draw. Every page is shown in the middle of the
screen (VID_MoveMenu), like DOOM's menus on the DS, leaving out the
cursor, which moves and spins, so the page doesn't wobble with it. The
Quake plaque on the left is left out. The quit question over a menu
leaves that menu where it is and goes in the middle of the screen.
---
